{"id":"city-loans-grew","title":"City housing loans that grew between Board files","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"After the Board approved a City loan for an affordable-housing development, did the same development come back for more?","finding":"5 developments returned to the Board for a larger City loan, $40,099,620 more in total than first approved. The largest increase was 4840 Mission Street (4840 Mission Associates, L.P.), from $18,510,000 in 2019 to $37,728,757 in 2023.","how":"Board files that state a City loan “not to exceed” an amount, grouped by street address. The first and the latest amount for the same address are compared; rises under 10% are left out.","limits":"An early file is often a predevelopment or acquisition loan and the later one the full construction loan; a rise can also reflect more homes, lost outside funding, or interest and construction-cost inflation. The comparison says where to ask for the budget history, not that money was wasted. Amounts, parties and dates taken from Board file titles are read by machine: in a hand check of 50 titles, 11 had at least one field read wrongly (4 after later fixes).","columns":[{"k":"address","t":"Development","type":"text"},{"k":"borrower","t":"Borrower","type":"org"},{"k":"firstYear","t":"First file","type":"year"},{"k":"firstLoan","t":"First loan limit","type":"usd"},{"k":"lastYear","t":"Latest file","type":"year"},{"k":"lastLoan","t":"Latest loan limit","type":"usd"},{"k":"added","t":"Added","type":"usd"},{"k":"rise","t":"Rise","type":"pct"},{"k":"homes","t":"Homes","type":"int"},{"k":"loanPerHome","t":"City loan per home","type":"usd"},{"k":"firstFile","t":"First file","type":"link"},{"k":"file","t":"Latest file","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"address":"4840 Mission Street","borrower":"4840 Mission Associates, L.P.","borrowerKey":null,"firstYear":"2019","firstLoan":18510000,"lastYear":"2023","lastLoan":37728757,"added":19218757,"rise":1.038,"homes":137,"loanPerHome":275392,"files":2,"file":{"t":"File 23